@startuml
title VirtualMotionTracker - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "External Control Application\n(User Application)" as UserApp

interface "OSC External Control Input" as OSC

package "VirtualMotionTracker" {
  component "VMT Manager" as Manager
  component "VMT Driver\n(OpenVR driver artifact)" as Driver
  component "Shared Memory IPC\n(JSON string exchange)" as SHM
  artifact "Legacy Controller Binding\nmycontroller.json" as Binding
}

package "Runtime Dependency" {
  component "SteamVR / OpenVR Runtime" as Runtime
}

UserApp --> OSC : provides external\ncontrol input
OSC --> Manager : FR-001 / DR-001

Manager <--> SHM : JSON messages\nmanager-to-driver /\ndriver-to-manager\nFR-002 / FR-003 / NFR-002
SHM <--> Driver : JSON messages\nsend count, handshake count,\nmessage length\nFR-004 / DR-003

Driver --> Runtime : via OpenVR\ndriver interface\nFR-005 / NFR-001 / C-001
Runtime --> Driver : loads / hosts\ndriver artifact

Binding --> Driver : provided as legacy\nbinding artifact
Binding --> Runtime : consumed for\ncontroller type mycontroller\nFR-006 / DR-004 / DR-005 / NFR-003

note right of SHM
  Bidirectional channels:
  manager-to-driver
  driver-to-manager

  Synchronization/control fields:
  send count
  handshake count
  message length
end note

note bottom of Binding
  controller_type: mycontroller
  mode: button
  parameters.sub_mode: complex
  Mappings:
  /user/hand/right/input/a -> /actions/legacy/in/right_axis1_press
  /user/hand/right/input/c -> /actions/legacy/in/right_a_press
  /user/hand/right/input/b -> /actions/legacy/in/right_grip_press
end note

note bottom of Manager
  Responsibility separation:
  external input handling /
  manager-driver shared-memory communication
end note

note bottom of Driver
  Responsibility separation:
  shared-memory communication /
  runtime driver integration
end note

note bottom of Runtime
  Dependency context:
  OpenVR SDK initialization,
  interface-version checks,
  shutdown behavior,
  path constants and SDK structures
  are constraints, not core product functionality.
end note

@enduml
